; ============================================================
;  SQUARED AWAY - THIS FILE IS NO LONGER READ
;
;  It used to hold two things, and both of them spoke in size classes:
;
;    A SHAPE  [amp_shape_...]   a silhouette of pockets, filled with
;                               whatever an armour happened to carry
;    A RIG    [<section>]       exactly these pockets, for one armour
;
;  Both belonged to the armour-derived rig - the mode where the outfit
;  you were wearing granted the pockets - and to the small / medium /
;  large / tall classes those pockets came in.
;
;  3.0 HAS NEITHER. A rig is an item, and its shape is four numbers
;  stamped on its own section:
;
;      amp_slot_2x2   amp_slot_3x1   amp_slot_2x1   amp_slot_1x1
;
;  put there by art/mkloot.py out of
;  configs/magazines/outfitloadouts/l_amp_rigs.ltx, which is the
;  balance file and the only one a human edits. What fits a slot is
;  decided by the item's own icon footprint and nothing else, so there
;  is no keyword left for a per-armour override to override.
;
;  THE FILE IS KEPT, EMPTY, ON PURPOSE. Another mod, a load order or a
;  leftover DLTX patch may still name it; an ini_file on a path that
;  does not exist is not something to find out about in a player's log.
;  Nothing in this mod opens it.
; ============================================================
